AB  - Artifact-centric business process has emerged as a representative paradigm of data-centric business process. As concerned in traditional business process, it is a critical issue to match business process models quickly, exactly and efficiently. Because of the pertinence between artifacts and tasks which deal with them, ordinary graph cannot describe the process successfully. Therefore, a bipartite graph for artifact-centric business process models is presented firstly, which can transform process model matching to graph matching. Secondly, a novel method using matrix conversion to measure graph edit distance is also brought forward. Finally, a similarity matching algorithm named ArtiMatch was designed and implemented. Theoretical analysis and experimental results show that the ArtiMatch algorithm outperforms existing algorithms in a number of performance metrics such as execution time, precision and recall.
