AB  - Business processes play a central role in today's smart applications. To become even smarter, they should be flexible, executable and measurable for adapting to changing demand, being enacted effectively and assessed precisely. Due to the fact that de-facto process modeling languages do not cover these properties, this limitation gives rise to substantial amount of work for the extensions of the mainstream process modeling languages. The existing extensions support to capture the other perspectives of processes (e.g., resource allocation, performance measurement). Focusing on data flow aspect, we propose a framework for augmenting a control flow process model to yield an artifact-centric process model based on the state machine and business artifacts. The proposed mechanism is presented with the help of a real-life case study provided by our industrial partners.
